1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,511
Sakshya, by Team EigenThinkers, SUTRAM 2026, Problem Statement 03.

2
00:00:04,512 --> 00:00:12,425
One evidence graph. Three answers: Explain, Reach and Predict. Every conclusion traceable to its source.

3
00:00:12,425 --> 00:00:22,477
We sign in with a named account. Every action is tied to this identity in the custody ledger.

4
00:00:22,477 --> 00:00:27,905
Case 0147: a fake trading app fraud. 26 evidence files from banks, telecom, phones, chats, network and CCTV, all synthetic.

5
00:00:27,905 --> 00:00:32,308
The verdict comes with its coverage, hash checks and ledger status. Offence pattern supported, against every alternative including no offence.

6
00:00:32,308 --> 00:00:37,356
Explain ranks competing hypotheses and shows supporting evidence, contradictions and gaps side by side.

7
00:00:37,356 --> 00:00:47,834
Reconstruction: every record on one corrected timeline. The CCTV clock ran 5 minutes fast and a router log was in the wrong time zone. Both were corrected from shared anchors.

8
00:00:47,834 --> 00:00:52,789
Each link between sources is a tested likelihood ratio. Records from one origin, like a bank alert and the bank statement, count only once.

9
00:00:52,789 --> 00:01:14,468
We zoom into the graph to read the accounts, phones and devices the tested links connect.

10
00:01:14,468 --> 00:01:21,778
Click any finding and it opens the exact file, line and SHA-256 hash it came from, with the parser and its version.

11
00:01:21,778 --> 00:01:37,337
Investigators can add notes. A note is a recorded decision, kept in the ledger and never silently overwritten.

12
00:01:37,337 --> 00:01:45,754
People: identifiers merged only when no contradiction exists. Two people sharing a common name are never merged, and a suspect was cleared by travel time.

13
00:01:45,754 --> 00:01:56,245
The map shows device locations with their basis and radius. No base map is loaded, so no location leaves the server.

14
00:01:56,245 --> 00:02:00,756
Reach: the money trail hop by hop, with reconciled statements, cash withdrawals and what is still held.

15
00:02:00,756 --> 00:02:11,025
Switch to first in, first out, or replay the trail as it stood at any moment.

16
00:02:11,025 --> 00:02:16,503
The freeze list states its basis: a model estimate, or a labelled heuristic. No arbitrary default percentages.

17
00:02:16,503 --> 00:02:24,663
Predict: which phase the offence has reached and how soon cash-out usually follows, computed only on records up to the cut-off.

18
00:02:24,663 --> 00:02:29,973
Next requests are ranked by expected information gain: which subpoena would change the conclusion most.

19
00:02:29,973 --> 00:02:38,102
Evidence and custody: every file hashed at intake, read only, and a hash-chained ledger with signed checkpoints.

20
00:02:38,102 --> 00:02:44,253
An honest control case: a delivery dispute. Sakshya reports no offence indicated instead of forcing a fraud label.

21
00:02:44,253 --> 00:02:48,768
And a case that fits no template is reported as an unknown pattern, with its suspicious indicators.

22
00:02:48,768 --> 00:03:01,620
Validation on 30 held-out synthetic cases: 30 of 30 outcomes correct, every finding traceable, zero wrong merges, 174 automated tests passing.

23
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:09,189
A court-style report is generated with its own hash, written to the ledger.

24
00:03:09,189 --> 00:03:14,717
Sakshya. Where every trace connects. Source code: github.com/SAMEER-MLPROJECT/INV_TOOL_4

